                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On May 5, 1954, the Paraguayan Army deposed President Federico Cháves, and the
                    National Assembly thereupon named Tomás Romero Pereira, President of the
                    Governing Board of the Colorado Party, as Provisional President of Paraguay. He
                    served in that capacity until August 15, 1954, when General Stroessner, having
                    been duly elected on July 11 to fill the unexpired term of President Cháves,
                    assumed the office of President. Documents pertaining to these events are in
                    file 734.00 and 734.00(W) for 1954.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
